WEBVTT

00:02.336 --> 00:03.803
Legend has it that...

00:04.972 --> 00:07.338
...during the Heian Period, there were
men who fought with no weapons.

00:08.108 --> 00:13.444
They were known as the Men of
Carnage and they reigned undefeated.

00:14.915 --> 00:20.080
Their technique was called
the Mutsu Enmei Style.

00:33.200 --> 00:40.629
<i>The Age of Chaos
Mutsu Enmei Style Gaiden</i>

00:40.907 --> 00:46.743
<i>Rushing through my innocent
youth without a care in the world.</i>

00:48.282 --> 00:54.187
<i>This soul of mine is
so easy to influence.</i>

00:55.856 --> 00:59.622
<i>WORRY ABOUT IDENTITY</i>

00:59.726 --> 01:02.923
<i>WORRY ABOUT IDENTITY</i>

01:06.700 --> 01:13.765
<i>This is what I'm wishing
for as I sing this song.</i>

01:13.940 --> 01:19.776
<i>I want you to acknowledge
me, that's all.</i>

01:20.647 --> 01:27.917
<i>You smiled at me for
the very first time.</i>

01:28.088 --> 01:36.496
<i>Thank you so much, thank you
from the bottom of my heart.</i>

01:37.197 --> 01:38.858
<i>I'll never forget it.</i>

01:48.608 --> 01:52.044
<i>Age of Chaos
Mutsu Enmei Style Gaiden</i>

01:56.917 --> 01:58.680
A new era is upon us...

01:58.952 --> 02:05.255
They say the momentum of time
can't be stopped, not by anyone...

02:22.509 --> 02:25.137
The current of change
released by Ryoma Sakamoto...

02:25.245 --> 02:28.373
...has gushed forth in a mighty surge...

02:29.349 --> 02:33.479
And the power of the Bakufu,
once so overwhelmingly dominant...

02:33.620 --> 02:36.487
...has been steered
firmly into the past.

02:36.890 --> 02:41.156
But ironically, this was also
a shift towards the very thing...

02:41.261 --> 02:44.560
...Ryoma had tried to stop,
anti-Bakufu aggression.

02:44.765 --> 02:49.134
<i>The Promise</i>

02:54.274 --> 03:01.339
January 1868, the year Japan
would usher in the Meiji Period.

03:01.548 --> 03:02.606
Fire!

03:10.056 --> 03:14.493
Scarcely two months after
Ryoma Sakamoto's death...

03:14.661 --> 03:16.856
...the Battle of Toba-Fushimi began.

03:16.963 --> 03:20.023
This would eventually
spark the Boshin War.

03:20.934 --> 03:26.099
And the Shinsengumi could be
found in the midst of it all.

03:26.873 --> 03:30.434
Although they were able
to score minor victories...

03:30.577 --> 03:33.011
...they were no match for the
modern weaponry and strategies of...

03:33.113 --> 03:36.947
...the Satsuma-Choshu forces, who
had joined with the Imperial Troops.

03:37.117 --> 03:39.108
They continued to fall in battle.

03:41.488 --> 03:42.512
Hijikata!

03:42.823 --> 03:45.792
You're in danger! Please, get down!

03:46.059 --> 03:47.492
Hijikata!

03:47.828 --> 03:49.728
Let us retreat to Osaka Castle!

03:50.263 --> 03:52.697
The main Bakufu forces
are already on the run.

03:53.033 --> 03:55.263
It's only us now. There's no use...

03:56.670 --> 03:59.332
So we've lost, have we?

04:00.240 --> 04:03.641
No, the Shinsengumi hasn't lost.

04:04.311 --> 04:09.010
But it looks as though we won't
be able to stop the flow of time...

04:09.115 --> 04:11.413
...armed only with swords.

04:12.586 --> 04:16.181
Times have changed, that's the
problem.

04:17.624 --> 04:19.592
Shinsengumi, retreat!

04:20.193 --> 04:21.888
We're withdrawing for now!

04:47.454 --> 04:49.012
Ryoma...

04:49.956 --> 04:52.220
Times have changed.

04:52.392 --> 04:54.952
Actually, they're still changing.

04:55.862 --> 04:58.854
But you're not here to see it.

05:05.372 --> 05:09.308
Our dream was nothing but a dream,
eh?

05:33.533 --> 05:35.091
Mutsu...

05:35.435 --> 05:37.369
Have you lost your power?

05:39.472 --> 05:42.441
Oh, I had no idea who was behind me.

05:42.709 --> 05:45.337
Who knew it was you, Master Joukichi!

05:45.579 --> 05:47.740
So it's you after all, Mutsu?

05:47.948 --> 05:51.145
I thought it might just be
someone who looked like you.

05:51.418 --> 05:54.387
Because you looked so
weak, sitting there.

05:57.857 --> 06:00.519
For a moment I thought I could nail you!

06:00.727 --> 06:02.558
In the past, it was
actually more intimidating...

06:02.662 --> 06:05.028
...to see you leaving
yourself wide open for an attack...

06:05.131 --> 06:07.861
...but now I'm not afraid of you at all.

06:08.134 --> 06:10.602
I was just going to surprise you...

06:10.770 --> 06:13.898
...but since I had such a clear shot
at killing you, I changed my mind.

06:14.207 --> 06:16.505
Surely no one bearing the Mutsu
name...

06:16.610 --> 06:19.511
...would ever be felled
by an old man like me!

06:20.447 --> 06:24.110
You could have just
gone ahead and killed me.

06:25.752 --> 06:29.483
You may be right, I might
have lost some of my power.

06:31.157 --> 06:35.355
Right now, the Mutsu name
feels more like a burden to me...

06:42.235 --> 06:46.365
So is that why you've been
looking at Ryoma everyday?

06:46.873 --> 06:49.535
It's the sea that I'm looking at.

06:50.110 --> 06:52.340
That means you're
looking at Ryoma, right?

06:52.912 --> 06:57.474
I heard that Ryoma once
compared you to the sea...

06:57.617 --> 07:00.814
...but I'll bet that Ryoma
was like the sea to you, too...

07:02.055 --> 07:03.522
The sea, huh?

07:04.991 --> 07:08.119
Ryoma died much too young, didn't he?

07:08.228 --> 07:10.253
He was too young to die.

07:11.164 --> 07:13.689
So, what can I do for
you, Master Joukichi?

07:13.967 --> 07:17.232
It's kind of a stretch to believe
that you just happened on me here!

07:18.872 --> 07:22.137
Well, after you came to tell us
of Ryoma's death, I asked you...

07:22.275 --> 07:24.004
...where you were going next...

07:24.110 --> 07:28.171
You said, "To look
at the sea," remember?

07:28.481 --> 07:31.507
And I've been wondering
how you've been, see.

07:31.818 --> 07:34.946
Then a friend of mine
happened to mention that...

07:35.055 --> 07:39.287
...he'd seen a man gazing
at the sea everyday...

07:40.593 --> 07:43.391
So how long do you plan
to look out at the sea?

07:46.933 --> 07:48.730
Until I've had enough.

07:49.602 --> 07:51.661
I suppose that's not a bad thing...

07:52.439 --> 07:55.602
Isn't there someone
waiting for you somewhere?

08:02.615 --> 08:04.207
If there's no one in your life...

08:05.685 --> 08:11.624
Listen, how would you feel about
taking my Sanako as your wife?

08:13.026 --> 08:16.723
Sure, I'm just an old geezer,
full of crackpot ideas...

08:16.896 --> 08:22.732
...but I wanted to ask if you'd do this,
that's why I've been looking for you.

08:26.806 --> 08:29.934
Miss Sanako is already
married, you know...

08:30.543 --> 08:32.773
...to Ryoma Sakamoto.

08:47.894 --> 08:51.955
It just pains me that I
can't do anything for Sanako...

08:54.968 --> 08:59.530
But I guess if that's how you feel
about it, there's nothing I can do.

08:59.806 --> 09:03.333
It's just that you were the
one man I felt I could ask...

09:09.349 --> 09:12.284
Now, now! You don't have to flee!

09:12.452 --> 09:15.080
I won't force you! It was nothing
but an idea this old geezer had...

09:16.322 --> 09:19.416
I just remembered a promise I made.

09:19.993 --> 09:21.324
A promise?

09:21.694 --> 09:25.653
When you said, "someone waiting
for you," that's when I remembered.

09:26.399 --> 09:28.424
Oh, I see! Is that so?

09:28.568 --> 09:30.763
So there is a girl waiting for you, eh?

09:30.870 --> 09:33.839
No. It's a man.

10:13.646 --> 10:17.776
<i>Edo, Imado-Hachiman</i>

10:37.604 --> 10:39.003
Lord Okita?

10:43.109 --> 10:44.508
Lord Okita?

10:44.611 --> 10:46.374
Should you be sitting
up in your condition?

10:46.679 --> 10:48.271
Hello, Miss Ran.

10:48.715 --> 10:51.741
The sunlight feels so warm and nice...

10:51.885 --> 10:54.854
Why don't you come sit by me
and we can enjoy it together?

10:56.990 --> 10:59.481
Actually, I guess you wouldn't want to.

10:59.626 --> 11:01.617
You can't risk getting ill too.

11:01.761 --> 11:04.093
You shouldn't come too close to me.

11:04.197 --> 11:09.066
Really, now! It might be tuberculosis,
but it's not always contagious!

11:09.269 --> 11:10.896
So, what brings you here?

11:11.037 --> 11:13.437
If you're here to check,
I just took my medicine.

11:14.207 --> 11:16.072
No, really!

11:16.743 --> 11:20.509
Since Dr. Ryojun told me to
look after you while you convalesce...

11:21.080 --> 11:23.048
I just stopped by to
see how you're doing.

11:24.550 --> 11:25.812
Thank you.

11:26.619 --> 11:30.885
Please, I'm just doing
my job, that's all.

11:31.324 --> 11:34.623
Still, you shouldn't come around
here more than you need to.

11:35.061 --> 11:38.861
Having you drop by so often,
I don't know how to deal with it.

11:41.234 --> 11:47.036
Just as I thought, you don't like
me either, do you, Lord Okita?

11:47.540 --> 11:49.770
Either? What do you mean?

11:50.376 --> 11:54.904
Oh, it's just that Dr. Ryojun and
his family do treat me very well, but...

11:55.381 --> 12:00.114
I never mentioned it to you, but
I'm sure you can tell by looking at me...

12:00.687 --> 12:04.020
You see, my father was a foreigner.

12:07.994 --> 12:11.987
My father went back to Holland,
leaving my mother behind.

12:12.332 --> 12:15.358
Not long after, my mother passed
away...

12:15.535 --> 12:19.130
At the time, Dr. Ryojun was
studying medicine in Nagasaki...

12:19.305 --> 12:21.705
...he and his family took me in.

12:22.508 --> 12:27.172
Whenever I walk down the street,
people turn around and stare at me.

12:28.014 --> 12:29.845
Well, don't you
think I look strange?

12:30.149 --> 12:32.674
Neither my hair nor my eyes are dark...

12:33.219 --> 12:36.620
...and I don't put up my hair like
other girls because I look funny...

12:43.029 --> 12:45.793
I know that I'd turn
around and stare, too.

12:50.903 --> 12:52.393
Because you're so beautiful.

12:52.638 --> 12:53.468
What?

12:53.940 --> 12:56.875
Would you go out and stand
on the porch for a moment?

12:57.010 --> 12:58.102
Certainly.

13:04.917 --> 13:07.647
Yes, it's just as I thought.

13:07.887 --> 13:10.117
You look beautiful, very beautiful!

13:10.356 --> 13:13.723
Standing there in the
sunlight, you seem to sparkle...

13:13.860 --> 13:16.192
You look just like an angel!

13:19.732 --> 13:21.723
No, you flatter me!

13:22.068 --> 13:23.865
Let me go prepare your medicine!

13:34.747 --> 13:37.375
I find it so hard to believe...

13:38.384 --> 13:42.787
That you're the man they call a
"demon"...

13:43.222 --> 13:46.953
The Captain of the First Troop of the
Shinsengumi, feared by all in Kyoto!

13:50.229 --> 13:51.628
You're looking at the real thing.

13:51.731 --> 13:54.427
The man before you is
indeed Okita the Assassin!

13:54.667 --> 13:56.498
Although I'm not a demon...

13:58.004 --> 14:01.462
I do know of one man
who is a true demon...

14:03.509 --> 14:04.703
Out of my way!

14:06.379 --> 14:10.645
He's still fighting,
to this day, I'm sure...

14:12.652 --> 14:14.643
Looking back...

14:17.256 --> 14:22.125
Those days I spent in Kyoto seem
like no more than a faraway dream.

14:24.797 --> 14:27.698
Who is this demon?

14:28.568 --> 14:34.564
It's Toshizo Hijikata, Deputy
Commander of the Shinsengumi.

14:35.108 --> 14:37.736
He's the true demon of the
Shinsengumi!

14:40.613 --> 14:45.414
I'm never going to see
Kondo or Hijikata, am I?

14:45.885 --> 14:48.718
Nor will I ever see him again...

15:02.401 --> 15:07.930
Ran, I believe that today will be the
last time I ever see Okita in person.

15:08.908 --> 15:10.899
I shall be leaving for Aizu.

15:11.210 --> 15:12.768
Dr. Ryojun!

15:16.082 --> 15:19.745
I'm afraid that Okita
is beyond saving now.

15:26.359 --> 15:29.385
I'm sure that Okita knows
that as well as I do.

15:29.595 --> 15:32.587
I'm asking you to stay
by his side until the end.

15:36.235 --> 15:38.066
Lord Okita!

15:41.340 --> 15:44.605
Okita, how are you feeling today?

15:45.444 --> 15:48.345
Now, now, that won't
do! You should be in bed.

15:49.248 --> 15:51.079
I had a dream.

15:51.884 --> 15:53.943
I dreamed about Kondo...

15:55.021 --> 15:59.355
It was a dream about Kondo
leaving Hijikata behind.

16:00.493 --> 16:04.259
Hijikata was shouting
at him not to go, but...

16:04.430 --> 16:07.297
Kondo just smiled at him sadly...

16:07.533 --> 16:10.832
...and then he walked
off into the darkness.

16:12.104 --> 16:13.731
Okita...

16:14.273 --> 16:17.401
Is Kondo dead?

16:22.381 --> 16:23.780
Yes, he's dead.

16:24.283 --> 16:28.413
On April 3rd, at Nagareyama in Chiba...

16:28.588 --> 16:31.751
Kondo surrendered himself to
the Imperial forces, alone.

16:32.458 --> 16:35.222
And yesterday, the 25th...

16:36.729 --> 16:40.096
At Itabashi, he was beheaded.

16:47.073 --> 16:50.509
Hijikata is still fighting, isn't he?

16:51.043 --> 16:52.510
He's in Aizu.

16:52.745 --> 16:55.680
He has joined the Bakufu
forces and is in command there.

16:56.349 --> 16:59.341
Up north, you say? Seems so faraway...

16:59.919 --> 17:02.012
If you have a message
for him, tell me now.

17:02.255 --> 17:05.122
I shall be headed for Aizu soon, myself.

17:05.291 --> 17:08.818
At this point, it's like committing
double suicide with the sinking Bakufu.

17:15.534 --> 17:19.561
"Please wait for me.
That is what Soushi said..."

17:20.206 --> 17:22.367
Just give him that message from me...

17:26.812 --> 17:29.975
Fine. I'll tell him, then.

17:34.353 --> 17:36.753
All right, then.
Ran, I'm counting on you.

17:36.889 --> 17:38.015
Yes, Doctor.

17:41.427 --> 17:43.122
I'll be damned...

17:44.163 --> 17:49.760
Who knew that Kondo would die before
me?

17:50.269 --> 17:52.203
I never would've guessed Kondo is
dead...

17:52.338 --> 17:56.468
...and Hijikata has gone north, to
battle on until the bitter end...

17:57.109 --> 18:01.375
Somehow it makes me feel as
though I've been left behind...

18:12.191 --> 18:14.819
Lord Okita, please don't die!

18:15.294 --> 18:17.592
Please don't try to
follow them into death!

18:19.398 --> 18:22.424
No, you're going to get
well, I just know it!

18:23.135 --> 18:24.568
So, please...

18:26.005 --> 18:28.565
That's right, I'm going to get well.

18:29.008 --> 18:30.976
Or rather, I'm going
to make myself get well.

18:31.544 --> 18:33.512
Because I made a promise...

18:34.213 --> 18:37.444
To cure myself of my illness...

18:37.917 --> 18:39.851
...and to wait for that one person...

18:42.421 --> 18:44.082
"That person"?

18:51.731 --> 18:56.668
<i>May 30th, 1868</i>

18:58.671 --> 18:59.968
Lord Okita?

19:01.340 --> 19:03.570
I have prepared your dinner.

19:05.544 --> 19:09.344
Lord Okita, you shouldn't
be walking in your condition!

19:10.583 --> 19:12.016
Don't worry.

19:12.184 --> 19:15.312
For some reason today,
my body feels light as a feather.

19:15.855 --> 19:17.345
Even so...

19:17.490 --> 19:20.482
Miss Ran, would you
please hand me my sword?

19:20.593 --> 19:21.582
What?

19:21.694 --> 19:23.127
Please, Miss Ran...

19:26.665 --> 19:27.996
Lord Okita...

19:30.536 --> 19:31.798
See that kitten?

19:31.904 --> 19:32.802
What?

19:33.572 --> 19:34.504
Oh...

19:41.046 --> 19:42.377
Lord Okita!

20:14.814 --> 20:16.805
This happens to kittens all the time.

20:17.183 --> 20:19.344
They can climb all the
way to the top of a tree...

20:19.452 --> 20:22.080
...but then they find themselves
unable to climb down.

20:24.290 --> 20:26.349
All right! Be on your way now.

20:43.242 --> 20:45.210
You've lost weight, Okita.

20:45.444 --> 20:47.537
Have you recovered from your illness?

20:48.747 --> 20:50.510
Yes, I've recovered.

21:15.608 --> 21:20.568
<i>To be continued...</i>

21:31.724 --> 21:43.761
<i>Those summer stars, I looked up at
them alone when I was a troubled child.</i>

21:44.036 --> 21:53.775
<i>My loneliness and the vast night
sky, melting and shining in eternity.</i>

21:53.913 --> 22:02.912
<i>I just don't know what this
dream means, if it leads to love...</i>

22:03.055 --> 22:13.727
<i>Even if it's just "hello,"
I want to hear your voice.</i>

22:14.767 --> 22:20.899
<i>The person I am today
is about to disappear...</i>

22:21.273 --> 22:24.299
<i>What is it that will hold me back?</i>

22:25.144 --> 22:31.413
<i>Will it be you? I won't ask you now.</i>

22:31.717 --> 22:37.212
<i>Maybe if we ever meet again...</i>

22:52.371 --> 22:53.770
On your feet, Okita!

22:53.906 --> 22:56.932
Get on your feet and show me
that strike of yours again!

22:57.242 --> 22:58.266
Okita!

22:59.745 --> 23:01.610
Next episode of the Age of Chaos...

23:01.747 --> 23:03.339
Like Snow.

23:03.482 --> 23:06.007
Pay close attention, and wait!
